# Build output
dist/
.astro/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Environment and secrets — never commit these. See ARCHITECTURE.md, section 3.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Google credentials, if anybody ever downloads any.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC (ADR-007). A service account key is a private key in
# a plainly-named JSON file that Google drops straight into your downloads, and
# the natural next move is to put it "somewhere the project can see it". These
# patterns mean doing that does not publish it to the internet.
#
# Note that the membership form needs NO credentials at all — Apps Script runs as
# the society's own account (ADR-012). If one of these files exists, ask what it
# is for; the answer may be that it should not.
*-service-account*.json
client_secret*.json
credentials.json
token.json
gcp-*.json

# Editors and operating systems
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
